tnumberx85.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#007D00;">code</span><span id="lstnumberx85.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#007D00;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx85.19" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#007D00;">blocks</span><span id="lstnumberx85.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#007D00;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx85.21" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#007D00;">starting</span><span id="lstnumberx85.22" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#007D00;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx85.23" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#007D00;">with</span><span id="lstnumberx85.24" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#007D00;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx85.25" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#007D00;">‘‘‘</span><span id="lstnumberx85.26" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#007D00;">python</span><span id="lstnumberx85.27" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#007D00;">.</span>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">function_signature</span> contains the function definition for the LLM to fill out, while <span id="A7.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">test_code</span> defines the properties (expressed as unit tests) that the resulting code needs to satisfy.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">function_signature</span> and <span id="A7.SS1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">test_code</span> both depend on if the game is a perfect or imperfect information game, whether it is being learnt in an open or closed deck fashion, and if the inference is perform via hidden history or hidden state inference. These variations are defined in the following sections.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, <span id="A7.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">orig_code</span> is the code being refined at each iteration. On the first
iteration, this paragraph is not present.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.2 </span>Perfect information games</h3>

